course: dictionary
lesson: 202
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. An albatross is a very large seabird with long narrow wings that can glide over the ocean for hours. «The wandering albatross has the longest wingspan of any living bird» is talking about a bird, because of the words wingspan and glides.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Long narrow wings are good for gliding, like an albatross's, and broad wings are good for soaring, like an eagle's.» The sentence compares the albatross with an eagle, so the clues tell you it is a bird.
explain: Some words also have a figurative meaning, which is not the literal one. «An albatross around your neck» is a problem or burden you cannot escape. To check, swap in your meaning, such as "a heavy problem I cannot shake off", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An albatross is a very large seabird, with the largest wingspan of any living bird, up to about 3.5 metres.
fact: Albatrosses glide for hours on the winds of the Southern Ocean.
fact: «An albatross around your neck» means a problem or burden you cannot escape.
fact: In an old poem, a sailor is punished for shooting an albatross, so the bird became a symbol of bad luck or guilt.
fact: In golf, an albatross means three under par on a hole.
exercise: «The wandering albatross glides for hours on the winds of the Southern Ocean.» What is an albatross in this sentence? | A fish that lives in rivers | *A very large seabird with long narrow wings | A small brown insect | A type of sailing ship
exercise: «Her broken promises were an albatross around her neck.» What does albatross mean here? | A large bird that sits on her shoulder | A type of golf club | *A problem or burden she cannot escape | A long wooden boat
exercise: «He scored an albatross on the ninth hole.» In golf, what does albatross mean? | A flag at the end of the hole | Three over par on a hole | *Three under par on a hole | A ball lost in the sand
test: «Long narrow wings are good for gliding, like an albatross's.» Which bird is said to have long narrow wings for gliding? | *An albatross | A sparrow | A penguin | An eagle
test: Which fact about albatrosses is true? | They live in the desert | *They have the largest wingspan of any living bird | They are a kind of fish | They cannot fly
exam: Read this: «The sailor's guilt felt like an albatross around his neck.» What does albatross mean here? | A sailing boat on the sea | *A burden or problem he cannot escape | A bird that sings at dawn | A sunny day at the coast
